{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqd7e4qngzi","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Decision: drop Cursor and Codex adaptor support (no per-session token accounting)","summary":"Decided to drop Cursor and Codex from the IDE adaptor roadmap. Neither exposes per-session token counts — Cursor's hook surface (beforeSubmitPrompt etc.) and Codex's hook schema (UserPromptSubmit, PostToolUse) carry no token fields, and neither has a public REST API for session-level usage. Provider-level APIs (OpenAI /v1/usage, Anthropic dashboard) are org-level daily rollups, not attributable to individual sessions. Estimation via tiktoken interception is too fuzzy to be trustworthy for cost accounting. Supported targets are now Claude Code (exact, JSONL transcripts) and OpenCode (estimated, chat.message plugin events). Cursor/Codex can be revisited if either exposes a session-level usage API in future.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T03:07:07.775Z","vec":[-0.100011445581913,0.013685115613043308,-0.05868636071681976,-0.04291101172566414,-0.004992419388145208,-0.03401528671383858,0.046945974230766296,0.0849461704492569,0.054791197180747986,0.03192691504955292,-0.051266297698020935,-0.05422312393784523,-0.03570420667529106,-0.002569003961980343,0.0665261447429657,-0.0283573679625988,0.005023869685828686,-0.027444390580058098,0.03388269990682602,0.020761797204613686,-0.04193101450800896,-0.03185361623764038,-0.010689129121601582,-0.033138375729322433,0.04747190326452255,0.008246299810707569,-0.01142334658652544,-0.09148673713207245,-0.012954874895513058,0.002013526624068618,-0.07153184711933136,0.06739471852779388,-0.023807384073734283,-0.03942757844924927,0.0014172480441629887,-0.041912857443094254,0.016748415306210518,-0.007907573133707047,-0.01322459988296032,-0.0199118684977293,0.00732331583276391,0.009367317892611027,-0.09705331921577454,0.03126637637615204,-0.02035968378186226,-0.06975184381008148,0.024641510099172592,-0.02955923043191433,-0.08663762360811234,0